      "refersTo": "upgrade-buy",
      "description": "An open progression row with segmented progress and a fragment purchase.",
      "html": "<div class=\"ds-upgrade\"><span class=\"ds-upgrade-icon\"><svg class=\"ds-icon\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"m12 3 8 3v6c0 5-8 9-8 9s-8-4-8-9V6l8-3Z\"/></svg></span><div class=\"ds-upgrade-copy\"><h3>Pulso persistente</h3><p>+4 de vida máxima al comenzar cada expedición.</p><div class=\"ds-level\" aria-label=\"Nivel 2 de 5\"><span class=\"ds-filled\"></span><span class=\"ds-filled\"></span><span></span><span></span><span></span></div></div><button class=\"ds-buy\" aria-label=\"Mejorar por 31 fragmentos\"><svg class=\"ds-icon\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"m12 2 3 7 7 3-7 3-3 7-3-7-7-3 7-3 3-7Z\"/></svg>31</button></div>",
      "css": ".ds-upgrade{font-family:system-ui,-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,\"Segoe UI\",sans-serif;line-height:1.55;color:var(--text,#ece8d8);display:flex;gap:15px;align-items:center;padding:13px 0;border-bottom:1px solid var(--line,#333a31);min-height:83px}.ds-upgrade-icon{color:var(--gold,#dbb66b);align-self:flex-start;padding-top:6px}.ds-upgrade-icon .ds-icon{width:20px;height:20px}.ds-upgrade-copy{flex:1}.ds-upgrade-copy h3{margin:0;font-size:13px;font-weight:500}.ds-upgrade-copy p{margin:2px 0 0;color:var(--secondary,#abb2a3);font-size:10px}.ds-level{display:flex;gap:4px;margin-top:9px}.ds-level span{width:21px;height:3px;background:#3b4337}.ds-level .ds-filled{background:var(--gold,#dbb66b)}.ds-buy{font-family:system-ui,-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,\"Segoe UI\",sans-serif;line-height:1.55;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;gap:6px;border:1px solid #69654b;color:var(--gold,#dbb66b);background:none;padding:5px 11px;border-radius:3px;min-width:62px;min-height:36px;font-size:12px;font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums;cursor:pointer}.ds-buy .ds-icon{width:13px;height:13px}.ds-buy:hover:not(:disabled){background:#dbb66b15}.ds-buy:disabled{cursor:not-allowed;color:#919780;border-color:#414a39;background:#161b15}.ds-buy:focus-visible{outline:2px solid var(--gold,#dbb66b);outline-offset:5px}@media(max-width:640px){.ds-upgrade{gap:16px}.ds-buy{min-width:59px}}"
    }
  ],
  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "The Lantern-Lit Expedition Journal",
    "overview": "Yala is an illustrated dark fantasy expedition journal. Charcoal stone, aged ivory and restrained gold frame a small traveler beneath monumental ruins. Painterly key art establishes the world; procedural stone tiles, illustrated characters and fog of war carry that world into play.\n\nThe interface feels deliberate and weathered without sacrificing tactical clarity. Heritage manuscript headings give names and discoveries weight, while compact system typography keeps resources, intentions and actions readable. Thin dividers and recessed tones organize the journal; light belongs to the lantern and the next meaningful choice.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Painterly fantasy imagery with a vulnerable traveler and monumental architecture.",
      "Georgia headings paired with compact system UI controls.",
      "Flat charcoal surfaces, ivory text, ember gold actions and jade energy.",
      "Explicit enemy intentions, adjacent resource information and deliberate turn feedback."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The Lantern Rule",
        "body": "Gold indicates an action, selection, progress or world light; large interface surfaces remain charcoal.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Two Voices Rule",
        "body": "Use Georgia for the world and system UI for the player's decisions; do not introduce another font family.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The World-Light Rule",
        "body": "Keep illumination inside the illustrated world; express interface hierarchy through tone and borders.",
        "section": "elevation"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "**Do** preserve the illustrated world and keep tactical information adjacent to the map.",
      "**Do** use Georgia for world names and system typography for controls and resource values.",
      "**Do** reserve gold for decisions, selection, progress and lantern light.",
      "**Do** pair danger color with explicit intention text, hatching or a visible mark.",
      "**Do** retain keyboard focus, labelled touch controls and reduced-motion behavior.",
      "**Do** adapt composition at the implemented breakpoints without hiding essential action descriptions."
    ],
    "donts": [
      "**Don't** add broad panel shadows, floating-card elevation or interface glows.",
      "**Don't** replace the supplied character illustration with generic decorative icons.",
      "**Don't** introduce additional typefaces or treat every label as a manuscript heading.",
      "**Don't** animate resource widths, add ambient animation loops or make enemy intentions depend on motion.",
      "**Don't** invent visible text fields or new component variants for documentation alone."
    ]
  }
}
